---
<WikiLayout language="en" title="The project" description="Muimenta Viva Wiki: resident onboarding and a guide to the village project.">
	<article class="prose">
		<h1>Muimenta Viva Wiki</h1>
		<p class="lede">Everything you need to live, create and share life here — and to understand how the project works.</p>
		<p><strong>Muimenta Viva</strong> is in the <strong>activation phase</strong> of the village of Muimenta (Carballeda de Avia, Ourense) — phase zero. It is not a finished co-living. We are still building, and we do not promise what is not yet in place. The spaces are rehabilitated, the network is growing, and the aim is to bring life back to the village.</p>
		<p>Few people live here day to day. A short stay or an urban practice is not the same as co-living life. There are too few people for this to be a co-living, and too much social mediation for it to be an artistic residency.</p>
		<p>The mission of this phase is <strong>social, gastronomic and entrepreneurial activation</strong>: open the spaces, welcome creators, build relationships with neighbours and create the conditions for a future village co-living project.</p>
		<p>On the ground, the project is coordinated by the local connector, together with <strong>Sende</strong> and <strong>Anceu Coliving</strong>.</p>
		<blockquote><p>This wiki is a practical guide for temporary residents and anyone who wants to understand the project without relying on internal documents.</p></blockquote>
		<ul class="home-links">{links.map(([href, title, desc]) => <li><a href={href}><span class="home-links__title">{title}</span><p class="home-links__desc">{desc}</p><span class="home-links__arrow" aria-hidden="true">→</span></a></li>)}</ul>
	</article>
</WikiLayout>
